{"id":"p13-l17","minutes":40,"summary":"Dead time, such as transport along a conveyor or a pipe, adds phase lag that grows without limit with frequency, which forces feedback to be slow, and a Smith predictor works around it by closing the loop on a model of the process without its delay. You derive the delay’s phase and its Padé approximation, implement a Smith predictor around a PI controller, and test that with an exact model the predicted loop reproduces the delay-free response exactly, shifted by the dead time.","html":"<h2 id=\"dead-time\">Dead time</h2>\n<p>A pure delay <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span> has transfer function <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: gain 1, phase <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span>. Unlike a pole, its lag keeps growing with frequency, so it sets a hard limit on crossover. A rough rule: crossover below about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span> unless you compensate.</p>\n<p>For analysis with polynomial tools, replace it with a <strong>Padé approximation</strong>. First order:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.363em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>which has gain exactly 1 and phase <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">arctan</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>: within 1° of the true phase for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span>. Note the right-half-plane zero, the signature of a delay.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-smith-predictor\">The Smith predictor</h2>\n<p>Let the process be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0991em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and the model <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.2835em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0335em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord katex-accent mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9579em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span><span style=\"top:-2.9634em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Feed the controller</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0301em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0835em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0835em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord katex-accent mtight\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9579em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span><span style=\"top:-2.9634em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>If the model is exact, the last term cancels the real (delayed) output, and the controller sees <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span></span></span></span>: the <strong>delay-free</strong> process. So</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.0463em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.1297em;vertical-align:-0.7693em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7693em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>the delay-free closed loop, delayed. The delay is moved outside the loop, where it no longer limits stability. You can tune the controller as if there were no dead time.</p>\n<p>The catch: a model error, especially in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span>, reintroduces the delay into the loop. Smith predictors need well-known, steady dead times.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"smithpred\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Step response of a process with dead time under the same PI controller, with and without a Smith predictor. With an exact model the predicted response is the delay-free one, shifted; mis-set the model delay to see oscillation return.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Process <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.2604em;vertical-align:-0.7693em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.4911em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7693em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>; PI <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.5</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span> s, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.5</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> cancels the lag.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Delay-free loop: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span></span></span></span>, so the closed loop is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>: a 2 s first-order response.</li>\n<li>With the Smith predictor: the same response starting 2 s late. Settling to 2 % at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span></span></span></span> s.</li>\n<li>Without the predictor, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span></span></span></span> has crossover 0.5 rad/s and phase <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">90°</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">57.3°</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">147°</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">33°</span></span></span></span>: a large overshoot.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">smith.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\ndt, tau, theta = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>\nKp, Ti = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>\na = np.exp(-dt / tau)                                   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># exact ZOH discretisation of 1/(tau s + 1)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">run</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">mode, model_theta=theta, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span></span>):\n    n = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt); nd = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(theta / dt)); md = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(model_theta / dt))\n    x = xm = integ = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>\n    u_hist, xm_hist, y_out = [], [], []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(n):\n        y = x                                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># measured process output</span>\n        xm_hist.append(xm)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;smith&quot;</span>:\n            fb = y + xm - (xm_hist[k - md] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> k &gt;= md <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># y + model - delayed model</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span>:\n            fb = y\n        e = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span> - fb\n        integ += e * dt\n        u = Kp * (e + integ / Ti)\n        u_hist.append(u)\n        ud = u <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;nodelay&quot;</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> (u_hist[k - nd] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> k &gt;= nd <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)\n        x = a * x + (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - a) * ud                          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># process (input delayed by theta)</span>\n        xm = a * xm + (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - a) * u                         <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># delay-free model</span>\n        y_out.append(y)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array(y_out)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_smith_equals_delayed_delay_free</span>():\n    y0, ys = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;nodelay&quot;</span>), run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;smith&quot;</span>)\n    k = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(theta / dt))\n    err = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(ys[k:] - y0[:-k]))\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;Smith predictor vs delay-free response shifted by <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{theta}</span> s: max difference <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{err:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>e}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> err &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(ys[:k])) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_better_than_plain_pi</span>():\n    yp, ys = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;plain&quot;</span>), run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;smith&quot;</span>)\n    os_p, os_s = yp.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, ys.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    iae_p, iae_s = np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - yp)) * dt, np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - ys)) * dt\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;plain PI: overshoot <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{os_p:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>%}</span>, IAE <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{iae_p:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>; Smith: overshoot <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(os_s, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>%}</span>, IAE <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{iae_s:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> os_p &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> os_s &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> iae_s &lt; iae_p\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_model_delay_error_degrades</span>():\n    ys = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;smith&quot;</span>); yw = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;smith&quot;</span>, model_theta=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>)          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># model delay half the real one</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> (yw.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) &gt; (ys.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_pade_phase</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> wt <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> np.linspace(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(np.degrees(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.arctan(wt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>) - wt)) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>\n    w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.3</span>; s = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * w\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - s * theta / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>) / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + s * theta / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>)) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n\ntest_smith_equals_delayed_delay_free()\ntest_better_than_plain_pi()\ntest_model_delay_error_degrades()\ntest_pade_phase()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A conveyor carries material 3 m at 0.5 m/s to a weighing sensor. What is the dead time, and what’s the rough crossover limit without a predictor?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3/0.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span></span></span></span> s, so crossover should stay below about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.17</span></span></span></span> rad/s: a closed-loop response of tens of seconds.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does the Smith predictor not help reject a disturbance that enters at the process input?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The disturbance only shows up in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span>, which still arrives through the real delay. The controller can’t react before the measurement changes, so rejection is still delayed by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span>. The predictor speeds up reference tracking and allows more aggressive tuning, but nothing can undo the information delay.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p13-l17\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"dead-time","title":"Dead time"},{"id":"the-smith-predictor","title":"The Smith predictor"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p13-l17-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase lag in degrees of a 2 s delay at 0.5 rad/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ωθ = 1 rad.</p>\n","answer":57.3,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase margin in degrees of 0.5e^(−2s)/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Crossover at 0.5 rad/s.</p>\n","answer":32.7,"tol":0.01,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Dead time in s for 3 m at 0.5 m/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Distance over speed.</p>\n","answer":6,"tol":0,"unit":"s"},{"id":"p13-l17-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Phase error in degrees of the first-order Padé at ωθ = 0.5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>−2 arctan(ωθ/2) versus −ωθ.</p>\n","answer":0.58,"tol":0.03,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p13-l17-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>With an exact model, the Smith predictor makes the closed loop…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The delay moves outside the loop.</p>\n","options":["identical to plain PI","unstable","the delay-free closed loop followed by the delay","delay-free"],"answer":2},{"id":"p13-l17-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The first-order Padé approximation has…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its zero is at +2/θ.</p>\n","options":["a right-half-plane zero","a double pole","gain that falls with frequency","no phase"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"smith.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndt, tau, theta = 0.01, 5.0, 2.0\nKp, Ti = 2.5, 5.0\na = np.exp(-dt / tau)                                   # exact ZOH discretisation of 1/(tau s + 1)\n\ndef run(mode, model_theta=theta, T=40.0):\n    n = int(T / dt); nd = int(round(theta / dt)); md = int(round(model_theta / dt))\n    x = xm = integ = 0.0\n    u_hist, xm_hist, y_out = [], [], []\n    for k in range(n):\n        y = x                                            # measured process output\n        xm_hist.append(xm)\n        if mode == \"smith\":\n            fb = y + xm - (xm_hist[k - md] if k >= md else 0.0)   # y + model - delayed model\n        else:\n            fb = y\n        e = 1.0 - fb\n        integ += e * dt\n        u = Kp * (e + integ / Ti)\n        u_hist.append(u)\n        ud = u if mode == \"nodelay\" else (u_hist[k - nd] if k >= nd else 0.0)\n        x = a * x + (1 - a) * ud                          # process (input delayed by theta)\n        xm = a * xm + (1 - a) * u                         # delay-free model\n        y_out.append(y)\n    return np.array(y_out)\n\ndef test_smith_equals_delayed_delay_free():\n    y0, ys = run(\"nodelay\"), run(\"smith\")\n    k = int(round(theta / dt))\n    err = np.max(np.abs(ys[k:] - y0[:-k]))\n    print(f\"Smith predictor vs delay-free response shifted by {theta} s: max difference {err:.1e}\")\n    assert err < 1e-9 and np.max(np.abs(ys[:k])) < 1e-12\n\ndef test_better_than_plain_pi():\n    yp, ys = run(\"plain\"), run(\"smith\")\n    os_p, os_s = yp.max() - 1, ys.max() - 1\n    iae_p, iae_s = np.sum(np.abs(1 - yp)) * dt, np.sum(np.abs(1 - ys)) * dt\n    print(f\"plain PI: overshoot {os_p:.0%}, IAE {iae_p:.2f}; Smith: overshoot {max(os_s, 0):.0%}, IAE {iae_s:.2f}\")\n    assert os_p > 0.3 and os_s < 0.01 and iae_s < iae_p\n\ndef test_model_delay_error_degrades():\n    ys = run(\"smith\"); yw = run(\"smith\", model_theta=1.0)          # model delay half the real one\n    assert (yw.max() - 1) > (ys.max() - 1) + 0.05\n\ndef test_pade_phase():\n    for wt in np.linspace(0.01, 0.5, 50):\n        assert abs(np.degrees(2 * np.arctan(wt / 2) - wt)) < 1.0\n    w = 1.3; s = 1j * w\n    assert abs(abs((1 - s * theta / 2) / (1 + s * theta / 2)) - 1) < 1e-12\n\ntest_smith_equals_delayed_delay_free()\ntest_better_than_plain_pi()\ntest_model_delay_error_degrades()\ntest_pade_phase()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}